    REFACTOR-0002: Phone hands each event to its current state
    
    Phone switched over its state in every event, so adding a state meant a
    new case in every method. Now OffState, LockedState and ReadyState each
    take their own case from every switch, and Phone holds one PhoneState
    and hands each event to it. Everything a locked phone does, including
    when it stops being locked, is in one class.
    
    Each state is given the Phone it belongs to. A state moves the phone to
    the next state by calling setState(), and LockedState asks the phone
    whether it recognizes a finger. Phone never checks which state it's in,
    and it doesn't name any state except the one it starts in.
    
    The output is unchanged.

